f a single-piece hydrophobic acrylic intraocular lens: new method for high-precision rotation control</article-title><source>J Cataract Refract Surg</source><year>2007</year><volume>33</volume><fpage>800</fpage><lpage>803</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17466851</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.jcrs.2007.01.030</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Becker</surname><given-names>KA</given-names></name><name><surname>Auffarth</surname><given-names>GU</given-names></name><name><surname>V&#x000f6;lcker</surname><given-names>HE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Measurement method for the determination of rotation and decentration of intraocular lenses</article-title><source>Ophthalmologe</source><year>2004</year><volume>101</volume><fpage>600</fpage><lpage>603</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15197576</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s00347-003-0951-7</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Viestenz</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Langenbucher</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Seitz</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Impact of the eye's cyclorotation on axial orientation analysis of toric intraocular lenses: recommendations for an optimized evaluation of rotational stability of toric IOLs</article-title><source>Klin Monatsbl Augenheilkd</source><year>2006</year><volume>223</volume><fpage>134</fpage><lpage>140</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16485225</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1055/s-2005-858715</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Viestenz</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Seitz</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Lang